 "remarks": "Welcome to 64 W Broad Street, a legal three-family property offering approximately 3,100 square feet of living space above a full basement. This versatile income-producing property features two spacious three-bedroom apartments and one two-bedroom apartment, providing an attractive opportunity for investors and owner-occupants alike. Ideally situated just steps from downtown Stamford and UCONN Stamford, the property benefits from a highly desirable location with convenient access to restaurants, shopping, public transportation, and the city's vibrant employment and educational centers.  All utilities are separately metered, helping minimize landlord expenses and maximize operating efficiency. With one apartment currently vacant, this property presents an especially attractive opportunity for an owner-occupant to live in one unit while collecting rental income from the other two apartments, helping offset monthly housing expenses. Investors will also appreciate the flexibility to establish market rents on the vacant unit and maximize the property's income potential.  Whether you're expanding your investment portfolio or looking to own a home while generating rental income, this is an outstanding opportunity in one of New England's most dynamic rental markets.",
